      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It appears a similar post was closed due to it not existing in .NET Framework 4.x. It is available in Standard 2.1 which Unity supports but the UdonVM could be running on Framework 4.x.\n\nIt would be nice if there was at the least a helper function for IsFinite since that can assist when a graph program is hitting memory limits in the editor.\n\nhttps://vrchat.canny.io/udon/p/isfinite-missing-from-single-and-double",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-12-25T04:36:38.866Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "`IsFinite` can be substituted with the already exposed `IsNaN` and `IsInfinity` but `IsSubnormal` and `IsNormal` cannot be substituted accurately.\n\nSubnormal is used to check if a value is so small it starts to lose precision (a value working with values smaller than the smallest positive value of a float/double).\n\nI'm not sure why `IsFinite` isn't exposed but `IsNaN` and `IsInfinity` are.",
